// `index N of C morton (x, y, z) [bits b] [leaf l] [wrap s]`: its queries
// against a grid's on the same dots, clustered, in a box that wraps, and
// of whole numbers in two sides (the nearest by how far); and its cells
// as laid out. The same on one core and on all.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/morton.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/morton.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAME --input-file=%t.one
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/morton_wrap.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.wrap
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/morton_wrap.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.wrap.all
// RUN: cmp %t.wrap %t.wrap.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRAP --input-file=%t.wrap
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/morton_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.whole
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/morton_whole.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.whole.all
// RUN: cmp %t.whole %t.whole.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE --input-file=%t.whole
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/morton_cells.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CELLS

// SAME:  near 0 differ, between 0, nearest 0; pairs 2636028, after me 1318014
// WRAP:  near 0 differ, between 0, nearest 0; pairs 321288, after me 160644
// WHOLE: near 0 differ, between 0, nearest 0; pairs 121676, after me 60838
// CELLS: 3000 rows, 2119 cells, visited 2119, 1708 leaves holding 3000 rows, 0 bad, 0 out of order
